{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "25", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "06", "M": "24", "S": "26"}}, "news": [{"title": "Gurugram: 450 families in Imperia Esfera rely on diesel generator set as snag sparks outages", "para": "The inhabitants of Imperia Esfera in Gurgaon are facing an ongoing nightmare of power outages that have persisted for three days, impacting about 450 residences. Continuous electrical issues have rendered their temporary 11-kV power connection inefficient. In a bid for clarity and permanence, residents are calling for a collaborative investigation to pinpoint responsibility.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/gurugram-450-families-in-imperia-esfera-rely-on-diesel-generator-set-as-snag-sparks-outages/133493654?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-72744/133493654.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Puravankara to jointly develop 7.83-acre land parcel in Bengaluru", "para": "Puravankara has entered into a joint development agreement for a 7.83-acre land parcel in southeast Bengaluru. The project has an estimated gross development value of \u20b91,100 crore and a saleable area of about 0.89 million sq ft.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/puravankara-to-jointly-develop-7-83-acre-land-parcel-in-bengaluru/133492205?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-322290/133492205.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Change in revenue record doesn't create, end property title: SC", "para": "The Supreme Court has established that mutations in revenue records do not establish ownership of property. The ruling quashed an order from the Madhya Pradesh High Court, highlighting that disputes over titles require evidence beyond mere revenue entries, which serve only fiscal purposes and do not imply rights. Civil courts retain the authority to ascertain the actual title while revenue entries are maintained separately.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/change-in-revenue-record-doesnt-create-end-property-title-sc/133491659?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-105034/133491659.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}